  "term": "osseous labyrinth",
  "definition": "The osseous labyrinth is the bony part of the inner ear in the petrous portion of the temporal bone. It is a set of connected bone cavities that contains the membranous labyrinth and includes the vestibule, semicircular canals, and cochlea.",
